y":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**Describe the bug**\r\nHere is an attempt to send a new follower notification no matter what the `followable_type` is.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/thepracticaldev/dev.to/blob/a9254eac407baf71a781fb94759b296f2fdedcdd/app/controllers/follows_controller.rb#L27-L35\r\n\r\nWhen `followable_type` is a tag, an incorrect notification could be updated or attempted to be created, cause the `notification_params` on this line will be `{ action: \"Follow\" }`\r\nhttps://github.com/thepracticaldev/dev.to/blob/a9254eac407baf71a781fb94759b296f2fdedcdd/app/models/notification.rb#L30\r\n\r\n**To Reproduce**\r\nI modified the `create_follow` spec to run delayed jobs so that it would be clear that it's failing.\r\nhttps://github.com/lightalloy/dev.to/commit/27ac0010866d1d5a4794e89f44d32a15c7114dd3\r\n\r\n**Expected behavior**\r\nOnly try to send a notification when a followable is a User or an Organization. At least add checks to the controller.\r\n\r\n**Additional context**\r\nI've started to refactor `send_new_follower_notification` in this pr #2030, but it makes sense to fix the described issue first. I'll add more checks for the valid arguments there.\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"lightalloy","id":30115,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMTE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30115?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lightalloy","html_url":"https://github.com/lightalloy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lightalloy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lightalloy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lightalloy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lightalloy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lightalloy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lightalloy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lightalloy/repos","events_url":"https://api.g